---
// FAQ accordion on navy.
---

<section class="faq" id="faq">
  <div class="container faq-inner">
    <div class="faq-header">
      <p class="eyebrow faq-eyebrow">Questions</p>
      <h2 class="faq-title">Frequently asked, honestly answered.</h2>
      <div class="faq-rule" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="faq-rule-line"></span>
        <span class="faq-rule-gem"></span>
        <span class="faq-rule-line"></span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span class="faq-question">Is it actually weekly?</span>
          <span class="faq-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <p class="faq-answer">
          Yes. One issue every Wednesday morning, 8am Central. Weekends are for building, so if a
          week ever gets skipped, the reason shows up in the next issue.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span class="faq-question">What does it cost?</span>
          <span class="faq-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <p class="faq-answer">
          Nothing. No paid tier, no premium archive, no upsell. If that ever changes, existing
          subscribers keep everything they signed up for.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span class="faq-question">Who writes this thing?</span>
          <span class="faq-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <p class="faq-answer">
          Rohith Perumandla, an AI/ML engineer with four years in the field. 2 SaaS platforms
          shipped, 3rd in build. The newsletter is where lessons from real projects get written
          down while they are still fresh.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span class="faq-question">Is it beginner friendly?</span>
          <span class="faq-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <p class="faq-answer">
          It assumes you write code and ship software, but not that you train models. Jargon gets
          defined the first time it shows up, and every deep claim links to something you can
          verify yourself.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span class="faq-question">Can I reply to the emails?</span>
          <span class="faq-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <p class="faq-answer">
          Please do. Replies land in a real inbox and get read. Corrections run in the next issue
          with credit, and good questions often seed future issues.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span class="faq-question">Where do back issues live?</span>
          <span class="faq-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <p class="faq-answer">
          In the archive on this site, free and searchable. Subscribers get them by email first,
          the web archive follows the same day.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq {
    background: var(--navy);
    interpolate-size: allow-keywords;
  }
  .faq-inner {
    max-width: 680px;
    padding-top: 46px;
    padding-bottom: 110px;
  }
  .faq-header {
    text-align: center;
  }
  .faq-eyebrow {
    color: var(--sheet-ink-tertiary);
  }
  .faq-title {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    letter-spacing: -0.5px;
    color: var(--sheet-ink);
    text-wrap: balance;
    margin: 14px 0 0;
    font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 38px);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }
  .faq-rule {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
    margin-top: 24px;
  }
  .faq-rule-line {
    background: var(--sheet-hairline);
    width: 64px;
    height: 1px;
  }
  .faq-rule-gem {
    background: var(--sheet-orange);
    width: 5px;
    height: 5px;
    transform: rotate(45deg);
  }
  .faq-list {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--sheet-hairline);
    margin-top: 40px;
  }
  .faq-item {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sheet-hairline);
  }
  .faq-item summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 20px;
    padding: 19px 2px;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .faq-question {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    letter-spacing: -0.2px;
    color: var(--sheet-ink-secondary);
    text-wrap: pretty;
    font-size: 18.5px;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.35;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }
  .faq-item summary:hover .faq-question,
  .faq-item[open] .faq-question {
    color: var(--sheet-ink);
  }
  .faq-marker {
    flex: none;
    align-self: center;
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    transition: transform 0.3s;
    position: relative;
  }
  .faq-marker::before,
  .faq-marker::after {
    content: "";
    background: var(--sheet-ink-tertiary);
    margin: auto;
    transition: background 0.2s;
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
  }
  .faq-marker::before {
    width: 12px;
    height: 1px;
  }
  .faq-marker::after {
    width: 1px;
    height: 12px;
  }
  .faq-item summary:hover .faq-marker::before,
  .faq-item summary:hover .faq-marker::after {
    background: var(--sheet-ink-secondary);
  }
  .faq-item[open] .faq-marker {
    transform: rotate(45deg);
  }
  .faq-item[open] .faq-marker::before,
  .faq-item[open] .faq-marker::after {
    background: var(--sheet-orange);
  }
  .faq-answer {
    color: var(--sheet-ink-secondary);
    text-wrap: pretty;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0 40px 22px 2px;
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .faq-item::details-content {
    opacity: 0;
    block-size: 0;
    transition: content-visibility 0.3s allow-discrete, block-size 0.3s ease, opacity 0.3s ease;
    overflow-y: clip;
  }
  .faq-item[open]::details-content {
    opacity: 1;
    block-size: auto;
  }
  @media (width <= 640px) {
    .faq-inner {
      padding-bottom: 84px;
    }
    .faq-question {
      font-size: 17px;
    }
    .faq-answer {
      padding-right: 26px;
    }
  }
</style>
